<title>UK: Tarmac group gets go-ahead for UK hospital.</title>
<headline>Tarmac group gets go-ahead for UK hospital.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>British building firm Tarmac Plc said on Wednesday a group led by it had completed financing arrangements to build a previously-announced 100 million stg hospital in Kent, southeast England.</p>
<p>The deal is part of the government's Private Finance Initiative scheme, which is aimed at encouraging private sector involvement in big infrastructure projects.</p>
<p>The hospital, around Dartford, was expected to be fully operational by 2000, providing 400 beds. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
